module

public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.DifferentialGraded.RightModule.YonedaFullyFaithful
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.DifferentialGraded.RightModule.YonedaVerdierHom
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Localization.ShiftHomUniq

/-!
# The source side of [Stacks, Tag 09LK]: `K(C)` is a quotient of its own image

Let `C` be a differential graded category over a commutative ring `R`, carrying a
pretriangulated structure on its homotopy category `K(C)` for which the differential graded
Yoneda functor

`Φ = K(h) : K(C) ⥤ K(Mod^dg(C))`

is exact, and let `G` be a family of objects of `C`. Write

* `N = ⟨h_{G i}⟩` for the localizing subcategory of `K(Mod^dg(C))` generated by the
  representables attached to `G`, as in
  `StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/DifferentialGraded/RightModule/YonedaVerdier.lean`;
* `A₀` for the *essential image* of `Φ` — the representables and everything isomorphic to one;
* `Z = Φ⁻¹ N` for the objects of `K(C)` whose representable lies in `N`.

This file proves the statement the chain of [Stacks, Tag 09LK] needs on the source side: for
every localization `q : K(C) ⥤ DA` of `K(C)` at the morphisms whose cone lies in `Z`,
commuting with the shift, and for all objects `x`, `y` of `C` and every integer `n`,

`Hom_{DA}(q x, (q y)⟦n⟧) ≃ Hom_{K(Mod^dg(C))/N}(Q h_x, (Q h_y)⟦n⟧)`.

In the intended reading `C` is the differential graded category of complexes of an abelian
category `A`, so `K(C) = K(A)`, and `DA` is the derived category `D(A)`.

## Why the essential image, and not the triangulated envelope

`DGCategory.RightModule.yonedaEnvelope` — the subcategory called `A` in
`StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/DifferentialGraded/RightModule/YonedaVerdier.lean`, for which the
third link `DGCategory.RightModule.homEquivDerivedYonedaVerdier` is stated — is the *thick*
subcategory generated by the representables: `ObjectProperty.triangEnvelope`, which is closed
under retracts, as the instance `(yonedaEnvelope C).IsStableUnderRetracts` records. A lift of
`Φ` to `A` is therefore *not* essentially surjective, and cannot be made so: a retract of `h_X`
in `K(Mod^dg(C))` is an idempotent of `h_X`, hence by full faithfulness an idempotent of `X` in
`K(C)`, and splitting it is exactly idempotent completeness of `K(C)`, which is not available
— `K(Mod^dg(C))` has all coproducts and so is idempotent complete, while `K(C)` for an
arbitrary `C` is not. The retract-closed envelope is genuinely bigger than the image.

What the Verdier half of the third link actually consumes, though, is not retract closure:
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.isVerdierLeftLocalizing_localizingClosure_of_le` and
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.homEquivVerdierEmbeddingShift` ask only that the subcategory be
strictly full, triangulated, and consist of compact objects. The essential image of `Φ`
satisfies all three — it is triangulated because `Φ` is exact and full
(`CategoryTheory.Functor.essImage.IsTriangulated`), and compact because the representables are
— and for it the lift of `Φ` is an equivalence by construction. So the whole chain is taken
over `A₀` instead of over `A`, with the same Verdier criterion and the same proof, and nothing
has to be said about idempotents.

## What is still owed, and it is not here

The identification of `DA` with the derived category of an abelian category needs `Z` to be
the acyclic complexes. One inclusion is the hypothesis that steps 1 and 2 already carry
(`DGCategory.exists_isTriangulated_derivedHomReflector_yoneda`'s `hZ`): if `G` enumerates the
acyclic complexes then an acyclic `X` has `h_X` among the generators of `N`, so `Z` contains
the acyclics. The converse — `h_X ∈ N` implies `X` acyclic — is *not* proved anywhere in this
development. It is true, and the argument is not formal: `h_X` is compact, so by the
Neeman–Thomason description of the compact objects of a compactly generated localizing
subcategory it lies in the *thick* closure of the `h_{G i}`, hence is a retract of some `h_W`
with `W` an iterated cone of shifts of acyclics; full faithfulness
(`DGCategory.full_yonedaOnK`, `DGCategory.faithful_yonedaOnK`) turns that retract into a
retract of `W` in `K(C)`, and a retract of an acyclic complex is acyclic. The missing input is
the Neeman–Thomason theorem, not anything about Yoneda.

Everything below is therefore stated for `Z = Φ⁻¹ N` on the nose, which is what the Verdier
quotient of `A₀` localizes at, and never for an abstract subcategory of it.

## Main definitions

* `DGCategory.RightModule.yonedaImage`: the subcategory `A₀`, the essential image of `Φ`.
* `DGCategory.RightModule.yonedaLift`: the lift `Φ' : K(C) ⥤ A₀`, an equivalence.
* `DGCategory.RightModule.yonedaInverseImage`: the subcategory `Z = Φ⁻¹ N` of `K(C)`.
* `DGCategory.RightModule.yonedaImageQ`: the quotient functor `A₀ ⥤ A₀/(A₀ ⊓ N)`.
* `DGCategory.RightModule.homEquivYonedaImageVerdier`: the third link over `A₀`.
* `DGCategory.RightModule.homEquivDerivedYonedaOnK` and
  `DGCategory.RightModule.homEquivDerivedYonedaOnK'`: the displayed bijection, the second in
  the spelling the second link's hypothesis on `Q` is discharged in.

## Main results

* `DGCategory.RightModule.isCompactObject_of_yonedaImage`: every object of `A₀` is compact.
* `DGCategory.RightModule.isVerdierLeftLocalizing_yonedaImage`: `A₀` is left `N`-localizing.
* `DGCategory.RightModule.trW_yonedaInverseImage_iff`: a morphism of `K(C)` has its cone in `Z`
  exactly when its image under `Φ'` has its cone in `A₀ ⊓ N`.
* `DGCategory.RightModule.isLocalization_yonedaLift_comp`: **`Φ' ⋙ (A₀ ⥤ A₀/(A₀ ⊓ N))` is a
  localization of `K(C)` at `Z`.**

## Universes

Nothing is added to `StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/DifferentialGraded/RightModule/YonedaVerdier.lean`:
`C : DGCategory.{v, u} R` with the index type of `G` arbitrary, and the localizing closure taken
at `Type v` as there. The condition `C : DGCategory.{v, v} R` that step 1 carries through Brown
representability is not needed here, and neither is `Nonempty C.Obj`: the essential image of `Φ`
contains a zero object because `K(C)` has one, not because `C` has an object.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09LK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09LK)
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace DGCategory

universe v u r v' u'

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated
open CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty

variable {R : Type r} [CommRing R] (C : DGCategory.{v, u} R)

namespace RightModule

attribute [local implicit_reducible] DGCategory.K

/-! ### The essential image of the differential graded Yoneda functor -/

/-- **The subcategory `A₀`**: the essential image of the differential graded Yoneda functor on
homotopy categories, that is the right differential graded modules isomorphic in
`K(Mod^dg(C))` to a representable `h_X`. Unlike `DGCategory.RightModule.yonedaEnvelope` it is
not closed under retracts, and that is the point: the lift of the Yoneda functor to it is an
equivalence. -/
abbrev yonedaImage : ObjectProperty (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K :=
  ((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).essImage

/-- Any family of representables lies in `A₀`. -/
private theorem ofObj_yonedaObjK_le_yonedaImage {ι : Type*} (F : ι → C.Obj) :
    (ofObj fun i ↦ yonedaObjK (F i)) ≤ yonedaImage C :=
  (ofObj_le_iff _ _).2 fun i ↦ ⟨show C.K from F i, ⟨Iso.refl _⟩⟩

/-- Every representable lies in `A₀`. -/
theorem yonedaProperty_le_yonedaImage : yonedaProperty C ≤ yonedaImage C :=
  by unfold yonedaProperty; exact ofObj_yonedaObjK_le_yonedaImage C _root_.id

/-- **Every object of `A₀` is compact.** The representables are compact
(`DGCategory.RightModule.isCompactObject_yonedaObjK`) and compactness is closed under
isomorphisms. No triangulated induction is needed, because `A₀` is only the image. -/
theorem isCompactObject_of_yonedaImage {M : (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K}
    (hM : yonedaImage C M) : IsCompactObject.{v} M := by
  obtain ⟨X, ⟨e⟩⟩ := hM
  exact isCompactObject_of_retract (isCompactObject_yonedaObjK (X : C.Obj)) e.inv e.hom
    e.inv_hom_id

variable {ι : Type*} (G : ι → C.Obj)

/-- **Verdier's left localizing condition for the essential image.** Every morphism from an
object of `A₀` to an object of `N` factors through an object lying in both.

This is `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.isVerdierLeftLocalizing_localizingClosure_of_le`: the
generators `h_{G i}` lie in `A₀`, and every object of `A₀` is compact. The retract closure that
`DGCategory.RightModule.isVerdierLeftLocalizing_yonedaLocalizing` takes is not used by the
criterion. -/
theorem isVerdierLeftLocalizing_yonedaImage
    [Preadditive C.K] [HasZeroObject C.K] [HasShift C.K ℤ]
    [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor C.K n).Additive] [Pretriangulated C.K]
    [((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).CommShift ℤ] [((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).IsTriangulated] :
    (yonedaImage C).IsVerdierLeftLocalizing (yonedaLocalizing C G) :=
  isVerdierLeftLocalizing_localizingClosure_of_le _
    (fun _ hM ↦ isCompactObject_of_yonedaImage C hM)
    (ofObj_yonedaObjK_le_yonedaImage C G)

section

variable [Preadditive C.K] [HasZeroObject C.K] [HasShift C.K ℤ]
  [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor C.K n).Additive] [Pretriangulated C.K]
  [((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).CommShift ℤ] [((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).IsTriangulated]

/-- **The lift `Φ' : K(C) ⥤ A₀` of the differential graded Yoneda functor.** It is an
equivalence: essentially surjective because `A₀` is the essential image, fully faithful because
`Φ` is (`DGCategory.full_yonedaOnK` and `DGCategory.faithful_yonedaOnK`).

It is spelled as `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.lift` rather than as
`CategoryTheory.Functor.toEssImage`, which is the same functor, because the instances that make
it commute with the shift and be exact are stated for the former; the equivalence is then
transported from the latter, and that transport involves no shift. -/
abbrev yonedaLift : C.K ⥤ (yonedaImage C).FullSubcategory :=
  (yonedaImage C).lift ((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK) fun X ↦ ⟨X, ⟨Iso.refl _⟩⟩

/-- `Φ'` commutes with the shift, being `Φ` followed by the inclusion of `A₀` up to the
characteristic isomorphism of the lift. -/
noncomputable instance commShift_yonedaLift : (yonedaLift C).CommShift ℤ :=
  Functor.CommShift.ofComp
    ((yonedaImage C).liftCompιIso ((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK) _) ℤ

/-- The characteristic isomorphism `Φ' ⋙ ι ≅ Φ` of the lift commutes with the shift. -/
noncomputable instance natTransCommShift_liftCompιIso_yonedaLift :
    NatTrans.CommShift ((yonedaImage C).liftCompιIso ((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK)
      (fun X ↦ ⟨X, ⟨Iso.refl _⟩⟩)).hom ℤ :=
  Functor.CommShift.ofComp_compatibility _ _

/-- **`Φ'` is exact.** The inclusion of `A₀` is exact and fully faithful and `Φ' ⋙ ι ≅ Φ` is
exact, so `Φ'` is. -/
instance isTriangulated_yonedaLift : (yonedaLift C).IsTriangulated := by
  rw [Functor.isTriangulated_iff_comp_right
    ((yonedaImage C).liftCompιIso ((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK) (fun X ↦ ⟨X, ⟨Iso.refl _⟩⟩))]
  infer_instance

/-- `Φ'` is essentially surjective: it is the lift of `Φ` to its own essential image. -/
instance essSurj_yonedaLift : (yonedaLift C).EssSurj :=
  inferInstanceAs (((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).toEssImage).EssSurj

/-- **`Φ'` is an equivalence** `K(C) ≌ A₀`. -/
noncomputable instance isEquivalence_yonedaLift : (yonedaLift C).IsEquivalence :=
  inferInstanceAs (((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).toEssImage).IsEquivalence

/-- **The subcategory `Z = Φ⁻¹ N` of `K(C)`**: the objects whose representable lies in the
localizing subcategory generated by the `h_{G i}`. This is the class the Verdier quotient of
`A₀` inverts, read back on `K(C)` through the equivalence `Φ'`. -/
abbrev yonedaInverseImage : ObjectProperty C.K :=
  (yonedaLocalizing C G).inverseImage ((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK)

/-- **The quotient functor `A₀ ⥤ A₀/(A₀ ⊓ N)`**, the analogue for the essential image of
`DGCategory.RightModule.yonedaEnvelopeQ`. -/
noncomputable abbrev yonedaImageQ :
    (yonedaImage C).FullSubcategory ⥤
      ((yonedaLocalizing C G).inverseImage (yonedaImage C).ι).trW.Localization :=
  ((yonedaLocalizing C G).inverseImage (yonedaImage C).ι).trW.Q

/-- **The third link of [Stacks, Tag 09LK] over the essential image.** For all objects `x`, `y`
of `A₀` and every integer `n`,

`Hom_{A₀/(A₀ ⊓ N)}(q x, (q y)⟦n⟧) ≃ Hom_{K(Mod^dg(C))/N}(Q x, (Q y)⟦n⟧)`.

This is `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.homEquivVerdierEmbeddingShift` with Verdier's condition
discharged by `DGCategory.RightModule.isVerdierLeftLocalizing_yonedaImage`; it is the statement
of `DGCategory.RightModule.homEquivYonedaEnvelopeVerdier` with the thick envelope replaced by
the image. -/
noncomputable def homEquivYonedaImageVerdier (x y : (yonedaImage C).FullSubcategory) (n : ℤ) :
    ((yonedaImageQ C G).obj x ⟶ ((yonedaImageQ C G).obj y)⟦n⟧) ≃
      ((yonedaLocalizing C G).trW.Q.obj x.1 ⟶
        ((yonedaLocalizing C G).trW.Q.obj y.1)⟦n⟧) :=
  haveI := isVerdierLeftLocalizing_yonedaImage C G
  homEquivVerdierEmbeddingShift (yonedaImage C) (yonedaLocalizing C G) (yonedaImageQ C G) x y n

/-! ### The lift is a localization at `Z` -/

/-- **The two classes of morphisms agree.** A morphism of `K(C)` has its cone in `Z = Φ⁻¹ N`
exactly when its image under the lift `Φ'` has its cone in `A₀ ⊓ N`.

This is `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.inverseImage_trW_iff` for the exact functor `Φ'`,
together with the identity `(N ∩ A₀)` pulled back along `Φ'` is `N` pulled back along `Φ`,
which holds because `Φ'` followed by the inclusion of `A₀` is `Φ` on objects. -/
theorem trW_yonedaInverseImage_iff {x y : C.K} (s : x ⟶ y) :
    (yonedaInverseImage C G).trW s ↔
      ((yonedaLocalizing C G).inverseImage (yonedaImage C).ι).trW ((yonedaLift C).map s) :=
  inverseImage_trW_iff ((yonedaLocalizing C G).inverseImage (yonedaImage C).ι)
    (yonedaLift C) s

/-- **The lift composed with the quotient is a localization of `K(C)` at `Z`.** This is the
statement the chain of [Stacks, Tag 09LK] needs on the source side: `A₀/(A₀ ⊓ N)` is a
localization of `K(C)` itself, not only of the subcategory `A₀`.

The proof is `CategoryTheory.Functor.IsLocalization.of_equivalence_source` along the
equivalence `Φ'`, with `DGCategory.RightModule.trW_yonedaInverseImage_iff` matching the two
classes of morphisms on the two sides. -/
theorem isLocalization_yonedaLift_comp :
    (yonedaLift C ⋙ yonedaImageQ C G).IsLocalization (yonedaInverseImage C G).trW := by
  refine Functor.IsLocalization.of_equivalence_source (yonedaImageQ C G)
    ((yonedaLocalizing C G).inverseImage (yonedaImage C).ι).trW
    (yonedaLift C ⋙ yonedaImageQ C G) (yonedaInverseImage C G).trW
    ((yonedaLift C).asEquivalence.symm) (fun a b g hg ↦ ?_) (fun x y f hf ↦ ?_)
    ((Functor.associator _ _ _).symm ≪≫
      Functor.isoWhiskerRight (yonedaLift C).asEquivalence.counitIso _ ≪≫
      Functor.leftUnitor _)
  · refine MorphismProperty.le_isoClosure _ _ ?_
    rw [trW_yonedaInverseImage_iff]
    exact (MorphismProperty.arrow_mk_iso_iff _
      (Arrow.isoMk ((yonedaLift C).asEquivalence.counitIso.app a)
        ((yonedaLift C).asEquivalence.counitIso.app b)
        ((yonedaLift C).asEquivalence.counitIso.hom.naturality g).symm)).2 hg
  · rw [trW_yonedaInverseImage_iff] at hf
    exact Localization.inverts (yonedaImageQ C G) _ _ hf

/-! ### The source side of the chain -/

/-- **The source side of the chain of [Stacks, Tag 09LK].** Let `q : K(C) ⥤ DA` be a
localization of `K(C)` at the morphisms whose cone lies in `Z = Φ⁻¹ N`, commuting with the
shift. Then for all objects `x`, `y` of `C` and every integer `n`,

`Hom_{DA}(q x, (q y)⟦n⟧) ≃ Hom_{K(Mod^dg(C))/N}(Q h_x, (Q h_y)⟦n⟧)`.

The right-hand side is the Hom group that the first two links of the chain identify with
`H^n(ev_x (L h_y))`; the left-hand side is a Hom group of a localization of the *source*
category, and in the intended reading — `C` the differential graded category of complexes of an
abelian category, `Z` the acyclic complexes — it is `Hom_{D(A)}(q x, (q y)⟦n⟧)`.

Two steps: `CategoryTheory.homShiftEquivOfIsLocalization` compares `q` with the localization
`Φ' ⋙ (A₀ ⥤ A₀/(A₀ ⊓ N))` of `DGCategory.RightModule.isLocalization_yonedaLift_comp`, and the
third link over the image, `DGCategory.RightModule.homEquivYonedaImageVerdier`, carries the
result into `K(Mod^dg(C))/N`. -/
noncomputable def homEquivDerivedYonedaOnK {DA : Type u'} [Category.{v'} DA] [HasShift DA ℤ]
    (q : C.K ⥤ DA) [q.IsLocalization (yonedaInverseImage C G).trW] [q.CommShift ℤ]
    (x y : C.K) (n : ℤ) :
    (q.obj x ⟶ (q.obj y)⟦n⟧) ≃
      ((yonedaLocalizing C G).trW.Q.obj (yonedaObjK (x : C.Obj)) ⟶
        ((yonedaLocalizing C G).trW.Q.obj (yonedaObjK (y : C.Obj)))⟦n⟧) :=
  haveI := isLocalization_yonedaLift_comp C G
  (homShiftEquivOfIsLocalization (yonedaInverseImage C G).trW q
      (yonedaLift C ⋙ yonedaImageQ C G) x y n).trans
    (homEquivYonedaImageVerdier C G ((yonedaLift C).obj x) ((yonedaLift C).obj y) n)

/-- **The source side of the chain, with `N` written out as a localizing closure.** The same
bijection as `DGCategory.RightModule.homEquivDerivedYonedaOnK`, with
`DGCategory.RightModule.yonedaLocalizing` unfolded on the right-hand side.

This is the spelling that composes with the second link: `yonedaLocalizing` is a plain `def`,
so an instance binder asking for
`Q.IsLocalization (ofObj fun i ↦ yonedaObjK (G i)).localizingClosure.trW` — which is how
`DGCategory.RightModule.exists_reflector_homEquiv_yonedaObjK` states its hypothesis on `Q` — is
not discharged by the instance the folded form offers, since instance search does not unfold
the `def`. Compare `DGCategory.RightModule.homEquivDerivedYonedaVerdier'`. -/
noncomputable def homEquivDerivedYonedaOnK' {DA : Type u'} [Category.{v'} DA] [HasShift DA ℤ]
    (q : C.K ⥤ DA) [q.IsLocalization (yonedaInverseImage C G).trW] [q.CommShift ℤ]
    (x y : C.K) (n : ℤ) :
    (q.obj x ⟶ (q.obj y)⟦n⟧) ≃
      ((ofObj fun i ↦ yonedaObjK (G i)).localizingClosure.{v}.trW.Q.obj
          (yonedaObjK (x : C.Obj)) ⟶
        ((ofObj fun i ↦ yonedaObjK (G i)).localizingClosure.{v}.trW.Q.obj
          (yonedaObjK (y : C.Obj)))⟦n⟧) :=
  homEquivDerivedYonedaOnK C G q x y n

end

end RightModule

end DGCategory

end
